**Definition 2.1 (fixed calibrated support).** In the original live space
$\mathcal H=\mathbb C^5$, put

$$
U_+=\frac{e^{-i\theta_0}e_0+e^{-i\theta_4}e_4}{\sqrt2},
\qquad
U_-=\frac{e^{-i\theta_1}e_1+e^{-i\theta_3}e_3}{\sqrt2},
\qquad
V=\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb C}\{U_+,U_-,e_2\}.
\tag{QC.4}
$$

These three vectors are orthonormal. Let $f$ be the original orthogonal
absorbing state. The actual stopped-state algebra is
$\mathcal L(V)\oplus\mathbb C|f\rangle\langle f|$ when live/stopped
status is classical. A four-dimensional Hilbert embedding is
$V\oplus\mathbb Cf\subset\mathbb C^6$; its extra coherent matrix entries
need not be physically populated.

Let $g_+,g_-,g_2,g_f$ be an orthonormal basis of $\mathbb C^4$ and define
the fixed isometry

$$
Wg_+=U_+,\qquad Wg_-=U_-,\qquad Wg_2=e_2,\qquad Wg_f=f.
\tag{QC.5}
$$

It depends on the calibrated preparation phases, not on $\beta$, $m$,
an unknown waveform or a learned probability law. Set $P=WW^\dagger$ and
define whole-domain channels

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathcal E(\rho)
 &=W^\dagger\rho W+
       \operatorname{tr}((I_6-P)\rho)|g_f\rangle\langle g_f|,\\
\mathcal D(\sigma)&=W\sigma W^\dagger.
\end{aligned}
\tag{QC.6}
$$

